# SHIPPED WITH THE RUNTIME, on purpose (external review, v0.5.18).
#
# The documented install is "copy this .weavedoc/ folder into your project", and the project on the
# other end is usually a git repository of its own — with its own settings and, on Windows, the
# default core.autocrlf=true. This repository pins LF for .weavedoc/** in its ROOT .gitattributes,
# but a root file does not travel with a copied folder, so the pin stopped at the boundary.
#
# What that cost, measured on a fresh clone of a real mine: 97 CR bytes in `schema`, 381 in the
# entrypoint, the bin+schema fingerprint moving ea390a9e0fbc -> d1324e0a09b7, and `validate`
# reporting 372 problems on a mine that is clean. The parser no longer breaks on it (loadSchema
# reads a trailing CR as a line ending since v0.5.18) — this file is the other half: it keeps the
# BYTES identical, so `weavedoc version` fingerprints match across machines and the bundle manifest
# means the same thing downstream as it does here.
#
# Every file under .weavedoc/ is text the runtime reads or a shebang script it executes.
* text eol=lf
